 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 507838,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Solve the formula <span data-math=\"V = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi {r^2} h\">V = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi {r^2}h</span> for <span data-math=\"h\">h</span>. This formula is used to calculate the volume <span data-math=\"V\">V</span> of a right circular cone with radius <span data-math=\"r\"></span> and height <span data-math=\"h\">h</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"V = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi {r^2}h\"></span></p>\n<p>Treat <i>h</i> as the variable and everything else as “constants.”</p>\n<p>You can skip to Step 4: Make the coefficient of the variable term equal to 1.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"3V = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi {r^2}h\\left( 3 \\right)\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"3V = \\pi {r^2}h\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{3V}}{{\\pi {r^2}}} = \\frac{{\\pi {r^2}h}}{{\\pi {r^2}}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{3V}}{{\\pi {r^2}}} = h\"></span></p>\n<p>Alternate answer option: <span data-math=\"h = \\frac{{3V}}{{\\pi {r^2}}}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"h = \\frac{{3V}}{{\\pi {r^2}}}\">h = \\frac{{3V}}{{\\pi {r^2}}}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
